        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Ames–Florida House, Alberta, Canada, New York, Cincinnati\n- Topics: Construction dates, Ordovician bentonite layers, Deicke and Millbrig ash beds\n\nFacts:\n- Ames–Florida House was built in 1856.\n- Ames–Florida House is in Cincinnati, a U.S. city located between New York and Alberta, Canada, in the clue’s framing.\n- The Deicke and Millbrig bentonite layers were formed during the Ordovician.\n- Cincinnati was the city most affected during the era in which the Deicke and Millbrig bentonite layers were formed.",
